  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launched in Q3 2023 with a $2M budget. Key developments include securing a strategic partnership with TechInnovate, achieving a 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms, and completing the testing phase for a secure file-sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Upcoming activities include a kickoff meeting on July 15th, a team meeting on August 1st to discuss budget allocations, a meeting on August 5th to discuss initial findings, an onboarding session for new members on September 10th, UI enhancements starting in October, a milestone celebration on October 10th, and a deadline for stakeholder feedback by the end of November."
